schema: spec-driven

context: |
  Project: <name> - <one-line purpose>.
  Capabilities: <list>.
  Stack: <languages, frameworks, database>.
  Sources of truth: <for example live frontend, ERD, client confirmations>.
  Boundaries: <what this project owns and what it must not own>.
  LLM boundary (if llm): deterministic code computes facts; the model interprets.

rules:
  proposal:
    - State the Expected Outcome as an observable result for the user or owner.
    - List Non-goals.
    - State whether the change adds a project capability and which standards that requires.
  design:
    - Number each decision and record rejected alternatives with reasons.
    - Describe data, API, and failure behaviour; include migration and rollback when data changes.
  tasks:
    - Group tasks in phases; end each phase with an "Expected Result" line.
    - Every task names the evidence that proves it (command, test, HTTP or browser check).
    - Track owner production confirmation in PROJECT_STATE.md, not as an open task.
    - The final task pushes the branch and reports the compare link.
